# QSAR Classification Model for VX‑hAChE Reactivation by Oximes

This repository documents, and allows full reproduction of, a binary QSAR model that
discriminates **high vs. low reactivation activity** of oxime-type compounds against
VX-inhibited human acetylcholinesterase (hAChE).

The model uses **7 quantum-chemical / physicochemical descriptors + 1024-bit Morgan
circular fingerprints**, and the final predictor is a **grid-search-optimized Random
Forest classifier**. Validation covers stratified 5-fold cross-validation, an
independent test set, Y-scrambling permutation testing, multi-seed stability analysis,
Tanimoto-based applicability domain (AD), SHAP interpretation and a 7-model comparison.

---

## 1. Repository layout

```
.
├── data_file_LUMO_HOMO_gap_126_freeTotalScore_N_natural_charge_free_pKa.xlsx   # training data (129 compounds)
├── WZ_redesigned_compounds_7_features.xlsx                                     # external screening set (79 rows, 77 valid)
├── train_qsar_binary.py        # training / validation / plotting script
├── predict_7features.py        # standalone prediction script (wrapper class)
├── rf_tuned_best.pkl           # final tuned Random Forest (main model)
├── standard_scaler.pkl         # StandardScaler fitted on the training split (REQUIRED)
├── ad_train_fps.joblib         # training-set RDKit fingerprints for AD calculation
└── README.md
```

### Data files

| File | Content | Size |
|---|---|---|
| `data_file_..._free_pKa.xlsx` | Training set: `Index`, `No` (compound ID 1–129), `smi`, 7 descriptors, `VX-hAChE` (continuous reactivation score, %) | 129 compounds, 11 columns |
| `WZ_redesigned_compounds_7_features.xlsx` | External screening set: `smi` + the same 7 descriptors, no activity label | 79 rows, **77 usable** (last 2 rows are empty) |

Training-set target `VX-hAChE`: min −1.98, median **12.60**, max 94.00.
Median split gives **64 positives / 65 negatives**.

---

## 2. Descriptor definitions

| # | Descriptor (training name) | Name used in screening file | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `HOMO-1` | `HOMO-1` | Energy of HOMO−1 (eV) |
| 2 | `LUMO_HOMO_gap` | `LUMO_HOMO_gap (eV)` | LUMO–HOMO gap (eV) |
| 3 | `Crash` | `Crash` | Steric/repulsion descriptor |
| 4 | `Polar` | `Polar` | Polarizability-related descriptor |
| 5 | `Molar Volume` | `Molar Volume` | Molar volume |
| 6 | `O Mulliken Charge` | `O Natural Charge` | Charge on the oxime oxygen |
| 7 | `Tot(D)` | `Tot(D)` | Total dipole moment (D) |

⚠️ **Column-name aliases.** The screening file uses slightly different headers than the
training file. They must be mapped explicitly before prediction (see §6), otherwise the
feature matrix is silently misaligned.

> All descriptors must be computed with **exactly the same DFT level of theory, basis set,
> charge/multiplicity and conformer protocol** as the training set. This information must be
> inserted here when the paper is finalized — it is not recoverable from the tables alone.

Sanity check (training-set ranges, useful to verify a re-run):

| Descriptor | min | median | max |
|---|---|---|---|
| HOMO-1 | −13.478 | −5.711 | −5.205 |
| LUMO_HOMO_gap | 2.922 | 4.194 | 5.305 |
| Crash | −8.170 | −2.380 | −0.280 |
| Polar | 0.000 | 2.290 | 4.050 |
| Molar Volume | 98.524 | 269.356 | 413.081 |
| O Mulliken Charge | −0.539 | −0.495 | −0.397 |
| Tot(D) | 0.3786 | 3.0481 | 8.5521 |

